{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowHabiroRigidity"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.q0_determined_by_sigma235_fibre_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.q0_determined_by_sigma235_fibre_data","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L108-L126","doc":"**§3b-cond conditional — the (2,3,5) fibre data forces the `q₀` observable.**\n\nIF Habiro rigidity holds over the (2,3,5) fibre-root index — the **hypothesis**\n`[HabiroRigidity H Sigma235FibreRoot]`, i.e. that agreement on the colored-WRT boundary data at the\norders-2,3,5 fibre roots is **sufficient** to determine the Habiro element — THEN two elements `w w'`\nrealizing the same `(2,3,5)` fibre boundary data have the **same archimedean `q₀` value**: the fibre\ndata forces the observable `W_λ(q₀)`, it cannot be tuned. Derived sorry-free from\n`q0_value_unique` (#3681).\n\n**Not established:** a **finite** root set does not in general satisfy Habiro injectivity; the class\nhypothesis is a strong, open restriction (carried, never instantiated). This states what *would*\nfollow — it is not a proof that the four computed roots pin `F_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.instFintypeSigma235FibreRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.instFintypeSigma235FibreRoot","kind":"instance","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L106-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.instDecidableEqSigma235FibreRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.instDecidableEqSigma235FibreRoot","kind":"instance","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L106-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.Sigma235FibreRoot.q1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.Sigma235FibreRoot.q1","kind":"ctor","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L105-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.Sigma235FibreRoot.p5m2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.Sigma235FibreRoot.p5m2","kind":"ctor","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L104-L104","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.Sigma235FibreRoot.p5m1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.Sigma235FibreRoot.p5m1","kind":"ctor","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L103-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.Sigma235FibreRoot.p3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.Sigma235FibreRoot.p3","kind":"ctor","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.Sigma235FibreRoot.p2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.Sigma235FibreRoot.p2","kind":"ctor","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.Sigma235FibreRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.Sigma235FibreRoot","kind":"inductive","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L97-L106","doc":"**The (2,3,5) fibre-root index.** The five roots at which the candidate `F_λ` is evaluated: the\norder-2 root `i`, the order-3 root `e^{iπ/3}`, the two order-5 Galois roots `e^{iπ/5}, e^{2iπ/5}`, and\nthe trivial `q = 1`. A **finite** index — the idealization at the heart of the honest-scope caveat. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.sigma235_p3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.sigma235_p3","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L84-L95","doc":"**Order-3 fibre root `ζ = e^{iπ/3}`.** Characters `[mark]_{e^{iπ/3}}` for marks `1,2,3,4,5,6,4,2,3`\nare `1,1,0,−1,−1,0,−1,1,0`, squared `1,1,0,1,1,0,1,1,0`; `D² = 6`;\n`F = [1/6,1/6,0,1/6,1/6,0,1/6,1/6,0]`, `Σ F = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.sigma235_p2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.sigma235_p2","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L71-L82","doc":"**Order-2 fibre root `ζ = e^{iπ/2} = i`.** Characters `[mark]_i` for marks `1,2,3,4,5,6,4,2,3`\nare `1,0,−1,0,1,0,0,0,−1`, squared `1,0,1,0,1,0,0,0,1`; `D² = 4`; `F = [1/4,0,1/4,0,1/4,0,0,0,1/4]`,\n`Σ F = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.hnorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.hnorm","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L69-L69","doc":"**CONTENT — normalization.** `Σ_λ F_λ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.hF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.hF","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L67-L67","doc":"`F` is the per-node quotient of the squared characters by `D²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.F","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.F","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L65-L65","doc":"The Verlinde weights `F_λ = [mark λ]²_ζ / D²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.hD2ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.hD2ne","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L63-L63","doc":"`D² ≠ 0` (the Verlinde weights are well-defined). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.hD2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.hD2","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L61-L61","doc":"`D²` is the node-sum of the squared characters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.D2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.D2","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The normalizer `D² = Σ_{9 nodes} [mark]²_ζ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.hlen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.hlen","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Exactly nine McKay nodes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.charSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.charSq","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The nine per-node squared characters `[mark μ]²_ζ` (marks `1,2,3,4,5,6,4,2,3`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.FoldedFibreBoundaryData","kind":"structure","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowHabiroBoundaryData.lean#L48-L69","doc":"**The folded fibre boundary datum of the candidate `F_λ = [mark]²/D²` at one fibre root.**\nContent-bearing: the nine per-node squared characters `[mark]²_ζ` (`charSq`), the normalizer\n`D² = Σ [mark]²_ζ` (`D2`), and the Verlinde weights `F` with the two genuine content fields\n`hF : F i = charSq i / D2` and the **normalization** `hnorm : (F.map id).sum = 1`. The normalization\nis the real (provable, non-trivial) claim — a bare marker `: True` would be a review failure. ","signatureChunk":0}]}